{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf to-fasta [-h] [--vcf-input VCF_INPUT] [-r REGION] [--sample SAMPLE]\n                               [--haplotype {iupac,alt,1,2}] [--uncalled {auto,n,ref}]\n                               [--include-filtered] [--mask MASK] [--chain]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --vcf-input VCF_INPUT\n                        Input VCF file path.\n  -r, --region REGION   Only build this region (e.g. chr21 or 21:30000000-31000000); default: the\n                        whole reference.\n  --sample SAMPLE       Sample to use from a multi-sample VCF.\n  --haplotype {iupac,alt,1,2}\n                        How genotypes are applied: iupac (default) writes heterozygous SNVs as\n                        IUPAC codes (e.g. R for A/G) and applies homozygous ALTs; alt applies\n                        every ALT; 1 or 2 applies that haplotype of a phased VCF (for unphased\n                        genotypes, the first or second allele, so 1 keeps the reference at\n                        heterozygous sites).\n  --uncalled {auto,n,ref}\n                        What to write where the VCF has no passing call: n (an N), ref (the\n                        reference base), or auto (default): n for a gVCF, whose reference blocks\n                        say which positions were called, ref for a variant-only VCF.\n  --include-filtered    Also apply variants whose FILTER is not PASS.\n  --mask MASK           BED file of regions to replace with N (e.g. low coverage).\n  --chain               Also write a chain file mapping reference coordinates to the consensus\n                        (indels shift positions).\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf to-fasta --vcf-input sample.vcf.gz --ref hs38.fa\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input stem>_consensus.fa.gz (+ .fai); with --chain, a .chain file.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, bgzip, samtools, tabix; minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
